<%# locals: (lobby:, showcase: nil)

    A CSS laptop (screen bezel, hinge, a thin base) showing the contests lobby,
    live: one row per contest from NextContest.lobby, drawn with the lobby
    table's own helpers (contest_status_badge, contest_prize_cell, dollars), so
    the names, status badges, prizes and field sizes are the real ones, and
    never a locked, cancelled or settled contest.

    MOSTLY SEEN, PARTLY COVERED. /turf-monster-v2 sets the laptop behind the
    phone, the phone's right third over its left bezel, and lets it run off
    the hero's right edge, which clips it (overflow-hidden on the hero
    section). So the screen is laid out for that sliver: the app bar and heading
    from the top-left (above the phone), then narrow stacked rows indented past
    the phone's overlap (pl-[5.5rem], header included), so every line sits in
    the part that shows. The full lobby table would put everything but the
    contest name off the visible edge.

    DECORATIVE AND INERT. aria-hidden takes it out of the accessibility tree,
    and `inert` takes the real table's links and row clicks out of the tab
    order and the pointer path. The figure's caption carries the text
    alternative.

    THE LIVE PAGE FIRST. With a contest being played or just finished
    (NextContest.live_showcase), the screen draws its live page,
    pages/_laptop_live, scaled from a 1280px canvas (0.33125). The lobby rows
    below are the fallback when there is none.

    EMPTY IS A STATE, NOT A BLANK. With fewer than lobby's limit of real
    contests, a row for the next drop (NextSlateDrop) follows the table,
    labelled with its date (or "Contests coming soon" once that date passes),
    so the visible corner of the screen is never empty. %>
<div class="w-[28rem]" aria-hidden="true" inert data-test="laptop-mock">
  <div class="rounded-t-2xl bg-neutral-800 p-3 shadow-xl ring-1 ring-white/10">
    <div class="aspect-[16/10] overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-page text-body" data-test="laptop-lobby">
      <% if showcase %>
        <%# The canvas: a hard 1280px desktop width, scaled to the screen's width
            (28rem less the 0.75rem bezels = 26.5rem = 424px; 424 / 1280 =
            0.33125). The screen is a fixed 16:10 box with overflow-hidden, so
            whatever runs past it is clipped. %>
        <div class="w-[1280px] origin-top-left scale-[0.33125]" data-test="laptop-canvas">
          <%= render "pages/laptop_live", showcase: showcase %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 border-b border-subtle py-3 pl-[5.5rem] pr-5">
        <p class="text-base font-extrabold text-heading">Turf <span class="tm-wordmark">Monster</span></p>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-heading">Contests</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted">Rules</p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-4 pl-[5.5rem] pr-5">
        <p class="text-lg font-bold text-heading mb-3">Contests</p>
        <div class="space-y-3" data-test="laptop-lobby-rows">
          <% lobby.contests.each do |contest| %>
            <% badge = contest_status_badge(contest) %>
            <% prize = contest_prize_cell(contest) %>
            <div class="card overflow-hidden px-2.5 py-2 w-40" data-test="laptop-lobby-row">
              <div class="-mx-2.5 -mt-2 mb-2 h-6" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary-700), var(--color-primary-900))"></div>
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-heading truncate"><%= contest.name %></p>
              <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs">
                <span class="badge text-[10px] whitespace-nowrap <%= badge[:classes] %>"><%= badge[:label] %></span>
                <span class="font-mono <%= prize[:classes] %>"><%= dollars_short(prize[:amount]) %></span>
                <span class="text-muted font-mono"><%= lobby.entry_counts[contest.id] || 0 %>/<%= contest.max_entries %></span>
              </div>
              <% if contest.locks_at %>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] text-muted">Locks <%= contest.locks_at.in_time_zone(NextSlateDrop::ZONE).strftime("%b %-d, %-l:%M %p") %></p>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
          <% if lobby.contests.size < NextContest::LOBBY_LIMIT %>
            <div class="card overflow-hidden px-2.5 py-2 w-40" data-test="laptop-lobby-next-drop">
              <div class="-mx-2.5 -mt-2 mb-2 h-6 bg-violet/60"></div>
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-heading truncate">NFL 2026 <%= NextSlateDrop::LABEL %></p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] text-muted">The next three-week slate</p>
              <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs">
                <span class="badge text-[10px] whitespace-nowrap bg-violet/15 text-violet-ink border border-violet/30"><%= NextSlateDrop.dropped? ? "Contests coming soon" : "Coming #{NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime("%b %-d")}" %></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="h-1.5 bg-neutral-600"></div>
  <div class="relative -mx-[3%] h-3.5 rounded-b-xl bg-neutral-700 shadow-lg">
    <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-0 h-1.5 w-20 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-b-md bg-neutral-800"></div>
  </div>
</div>
